00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.350
Uh, Dr.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.030
Krashen is very transparent.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.650
You can go to his website uh, I think
it's sdkrashen.com and there's a lot

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.480
of free material available there.

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:20.549
But as you know, he, he stresses the
fact that we learn through input.

00:02:20.579 --> 00:02:23.190
We learn through compelling,
comprehensible input.

00:02:23.429 --> 00:02:28.859
We learn through meaningful messages and
some people may claim that that's not the

00:02:28.859 --> 00:02:33.450
whole story that we also have to speak
and that some people, uh, can read and,

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:37.670
and can, can, uh, you know, have high
comprehension, but are afraid to speak.

00:02:38.149 --> 00:02:41.070
BUt if people are afraid to
speak, they're gonna be even more

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.540
afraid if they don't understand.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:46.770
So I just feel that everything he
said about language acquisition

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.210
matched my experience in learning the
languages that I learned throughout

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.190
my first, my professional career.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:58.560
And then when I got more interested in
